1
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:10,280
Have you heard anything from Mom?

2
00:03:11,040 --> 00:03:13,880
Don't talk about her anymore.
We all have to bear our own choices.

3
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:16,600
If you run from me, I'll kill you.

4
00:03:16,680 --> 00:03:18,000
If you still love me,

5
00:03:19,120 --> 00:03:21,680
then go live your own life.

6
00:03:21,760 --> 00:03:23,400
Goodbye, Mom.

7
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:26,880
Mom, where are you?

8
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:28,560
Grandma and I will come get you.

9
00:03:28,640 --> 00:03:30,920
-Don't! Mom!
-Grandma!

10
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:32,720
-Grandma!
-Mom!

11
00:03:33,960 --> 00:03:35,680
Grandma!

12
00:03:35,760 --> 00:03:38,920
PREVIOUSLY

13
00:04:06,720 --> 00:04:09,560
You probably feel like your whole world

14
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:11,520
has collapsed.

15
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:16,959
It was like that for me

16
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:20,680
when my father left me

17
00:04:22,520 --> 00:04:24,480
and my mother started a new family.

18
00:04:26,640 --> 00:04:28,680
I felt

19
00:04:29,840 --> 00:04:33,080
completely alone, like I had nothing left.

20
00:04:36,440 --> 00:04:38,760
But I chose to keep living.

21
00:04:39,960 --> 00:04:41,560
I wondered

22
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:44,840
if maybe I just loved myself too much.

23
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:47,960
But that wasn't it.

24
00:04:51,840 --> 00:04:53,240
The truth is, I loved my mom.

25
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:57,080
I wanted her to be happy.

26
00:04:59,200 --> 00:05:00,920
I wanted to be able to take care of her.

27
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:06,200
None of us is born into this world
completely alone.

28
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:10,440
We still have family.

29
00:05:11,760 --> 00:05:14,960
And I chose to keep living

30
00:05:16,280 --> 00:05:17,400
for the people I love.

31
00:05:21,960 --> 00:05:23,880
I don't know how you feel about it.

32
00:05:25,320 --> 00:05:26,680
But I want you to know that

33
00:05:30,040 --> 00:05:31,200
I'll always be here for you.

34
00:06:42,160 --> 00:06:43,360
Hathaya.

35
00:06:44,760 --> 00:06:47,200
Death isn't something
we should only grieve.

36
00:06:48,160 --> 00:06:50,000
In a way, it can also
be something to celebrate.

37
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:55,840
Duangjai lived a long life.

38
00:06:56,360 --> 00:06:59,560
She experienced plenty
of sorrow and happiness.

39
00:07:00,960 --> 00:07:02,960
And the love you gave her

40
00:07:03,040 --> 00:07:05,840
allowed her spirit to leave
this world in peace.

41
00:07:08,280 --> 00:07:10,040
I'm speaking as an old man now.

42
00:07:13,160 --> 00:07:17,040
All grandparents want is to see their kids
and grandkids happy and successful.

43
00:07:19,160 --> 00:07:22,640
That's all we truly want.

44
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:29,200
I want Grandma to be at peace.

45
00:07:30,880 --> 00:07:32,640
I won't fall apart anymore.

46
00:07:35,360 --> 00:07:38,320
Take her urn upstairs to the prayer room.

47
00:07:41,320 --> 00:07:43,800
Duangjai was practically family to me.

48
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:47,680
Place her beside your father.

49
00:07:54,520 --> 00:07:56,400
-Let's go.
-Yes, sir.

50
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:55,640
Dad,

51
00:08:57,720 --> 00:09:00,240
please take care of Grandma for me.

52
00:09:09,920 --> 00:09:12,760
Dad, Grandma,
please keep giving me strength.

53
00:09:13,800 --> 00:09:17,480
I promise I'll be strong.

54
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:26,280
I'll make both of you

55
00:09:27,120 --> 00:09:28,920
proud of me.

56
00:09:56,520 --> 00:09:57,640
Don't go in there.

57
00:10:00,960 --> 00:10:02,440
That isn't your room.

58
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:05,400
I threw all your things away.

59
00:10:08,440 --> 00:10:12,680
And don't come upstairs again.
You're a maid, so stay where you belong.

60
00:10:28,280 --> 00:10:30,800
I'm not completely heartless,

61
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:33,960
but she still has more to prove.

62
00:10:41,480 --> 00:10:44,640
Madam. Madam. Madam.

63
00:10:44,720 --> 00:10:47,200
Would you stop bothering me?
Go do whatever you have to.

64
00:10:47,280 --> 00:10:49,960
If you have nothing to do,

65
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:52,520
go find a cat or dog to bathe. Go.

66
00:10:52,600 --> 00:10:56,000
Madam, please listen to me first.

67
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:57,640
She's here.

68
00:10:57,720 --> 00:10:59,280
Who?

69
00:10:59,360 --> 00:11:03,320
Hathai. Hathaya's mother.
She's already come into the house.

70
00:11:03,400 --> 00:11:06,480
What? Hathai? Where is she?

71
00:11:06,560 --> 00:11:08,280
Out front. Let's go.

72
00:11:09,760 --> 00:11:12,680
If you don't stay here, where will you go?

73
00:11:13,600 --> 00:11:16,760
I'll take her somewhere myself.

74
00:11:16,840 --> 00:11:19,360
Somewhere more appropriate for her.

75
00:11:20,200 --> 00:11:21,080
Liu.

76
00:11:21,160 --> 00:11:22,880
-Chamoi.
-Yes?

77
00:11:22,960 --> 00:11:25,320
Take Hathai's bag.

78
00:11:25,400 --> 00:11:26,720
Yes, madam.

79
00:11:28,680 --> 00:11:30,880
Chamoi, where are you taking my bag?

80
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:31,800
Chamoi.

81
00:11:31,880 --> 00:11:33,760
Somewhere you belong.

82
00:11:35,080 --> 00:11:36,720
Throw it out.

83
00:11:36,800 --> 00:11:37,920
That's my bag.

84
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:39,360
Chamoi.

85
00:11:40,920 --> 00:11:43,680
Outside this house
is where you belong. Get out.

86
00:11:44,280 --> 00:11:46,000
Ann, give that back right now.

87
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:47,520
It belongs to Ms. Hathai.

88
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:51,720
Liu. I know I treated you badly.

89
00:11:53,440 --> 00:11:54,840
I want to apologize.

90
00:11:56,080 --> 00:11:59,080
You think an apology
makes everything go away?

91
00:11:59,600 --> 00:12:03,080
You stole what was mine.
You caused my husband's death.

92
00:12:03,160 --> 00:12:05,440
Is being sorry
enough to make up for all that?

93
00:12:05,520 --> 00:12:09,360
Then what do you want me to do
before you'll stop being angry with me?

94
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:11,760
Kneel and bow to me.

95
00:12:11,840 --> 00:12:13,280
Right now.

96
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:20,760
Mom, you don't have to.

97
00:12:20,840 --> 00:12:22,240
Stay out of this, Hathaya.

98
00:12:22,320 --> 00:12:24,400
I don't mean to hold this over your head,

99
00:12:24,480 --> 00:12:26,880
but I've done enough
to protect you and Chayanee

100
00:12:26,960 --> 00:12:29,240
that you should be able to forgive us.

101
00:12:31,840 --> 00:12:32,920
-I'm sorry.
-Mom.

102
00:12:36,320 --> 00:12:40,000
Let me do this. You've done enough for me.

103
00:12:40,680 --> 00:12:42,400
Let me do something for myself for once.

104
00:13:26,480 --> 00:13:27,960
I'm sorry.

105
00:13:30,160 --> 00:13:32,080
And I hope everything

106
00:13:33,240 --> 00:13:34,720
can end here.

107
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:42,040
Come on, Mom.

108
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:46,920
You really have no shame.

109
00:13:48,680 --> 00:13:50,000
No conscience.

110
00:13:51,080 --> 00:13:54,960
No remorse. You're the reason
your own mother died.

111
00:13:57,280 --> 00:14:01,120
Hathaya loved her grandmother more
than anything. She did everything for her.

112
00:14:01,200 --> 00:14:03,120
But you were the reason

113
00:14:03,200 --> 00:14:04,880
Hathaya's grandmother died.

114
00:14:04,960 --> 00:14:08,120
You've been ruining Hathaya's life

115
00:14:08,200 --> 00:14:10,720
ever since you took
her away from this house.

116
00:14:12,280 --> 00:14:15,440
If I were you,

117
00:14:15,520 --> 00:14:17,440
I wouldn't have the nerve
to show my face here

118
00:14:18,520 --> 00:14:21,600
or beg my daughter for sympathy again.

119
00:14:25,480 --> 00:14:28,600
Mom, come see Grandpa. Come on.

120
00:14:40,560 --> 00:14:42,520
I don't want to be
a burden to you anymore.

121
00:14:43,120 --> 00:14:46,520
Mom, don't listen
to what other people say.

122
00:14:48,600 --> 00:14:50,400
But Liu is right.

123
00:14:56,960 --> 00:14:59,360
I took you away from this house

124
00:15:01,280 --> 00:15:04,120
and made you lose
so many good opportunities in life.

125
00:15:07,160 --> 00:15:09,040
I did terrible things.

126
00:15:12,400 --> 00:15:14,640
And I was the reason Grandma died.

127
00:15:17,520 --> 00:15:19,280
Just let me go my own way.

128
00:15:21,040 --> 00:15:22,760
Mom.

129
00:15:24,440 --> 00:15:28,120
If you love me, then stay with me.

130
00:15:29,320 --> 00:15:33,360
Whatever happens, you have
to accept it and fight through it.

131
00:15:35,840 --> 00:15:37,720
I know you feel guilty.

132
00:15:39,120 --> 00:15:43,120
Then prove yourself. Show everyone

133
00:15:43,200 --> 00:15:45,000
that you can make things right.

134
00:15:45,080 --> 00:15:47,080
Show them that you can change.

135
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:51,600
Mom.

136
00:15:54,480 --> 00:15:56,960
I'm not as strong.

137
00:15:59,080 --> 00:16:01,640
I need someone beside me too.

138
00:16:04,880 --> 00:16:06,520
Will you stay with me?

139
00:16:17,520 --> 00:16:18,720
Alright.

140
00:16:20,960 --> 00:16:22,320
I'll stay with you.

141
00:16:24,760 --> 00:16:26,440
I'll protect you.

142
00:16:50,600 --> 00:16:54,280
Mom, I'll take you to see Grandpa.

143
00:17:51,440 --> 00:17:53,800
What you did caused me tremendous pain.

144
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:58,280
I lost both of my sons.

145
00:18:00,640 --> 00:18:03,760
Even if you lay down
and died in front of me today,

146
00:18:05,040 --> 00:18:07,760
it still wouldn't make up
for what you did.

147
00:18:09,640 --> 00:18:12,560
I accept responsibility
for everything, Father.

148
00:18:13,680 --> 00:18:15,440
Don't call me Father.

149
00:18:17,880 --> 00:18:19,880
Whatever relationship we had ended

150
00:18:19,960 --> 00:18:22,440
the day you took your daughter
and left this house.

151
00:18:31,080 --> 00:18:34,600
If you won't forgive me, then I'll leave.

152
00:18:36,560 --> 00:18:39,080
Stop wandering around
and causing trouble for your daughter.

153
00:18:45,280 --> 00:18:47,840
I'll allow you to stay in this house.

154
00:18:50,360 --> 00:18:52,320
But only because you are Hathaya's mother.

155
00:19:00,520 --> 00:19:01,840
Thank you, Father.

156
00:19:04,160 --> 00:19:07,440
All I ask is to be allowed
to take care of my daughter.

157
00:19:11,080 --> 00:19:13,160
But I won't give up either.

158
00:19:14,400 --> 00:19:17,280
I'll wait for the day you can forgive me.

159
00:19:46,360 --> 00:19:47,600
I hate them.

160
00:19:48,480 --> 00:19:50,960
I won't let them live happily here.

161
00:20:05,160 --> 00:20:08,800
Listen, everyone. My son Raiwin
is candidate number one.

162
00:20:09,360 --> 00:20:10,400
Please support him.

163
00:20:10,480 --> 00:20:13,760
People of my generation have had our time.
Now it's time to step aside and let

164
00:20:13,840 --> 00:20:16,120
the younger generation come in
and manage our community

165
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:18,520
so it can continue to grow and prosper.

166
00:20:19,080 --> 00:20:19,960
For Raiwin,

167
00:20:20,040 --> 00:20:22,920
I am ready to give him
my full backing and support for him

168
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:25,120
as a new-generation leader

169
00:20:25,200 --> 00:20:28,240
who will continue
developing our community.

170
00:20:28,920 --> 00:20:32,680
Some reports say Mr. Saksit
put you forward as his proxy.

171
00:20:32,760 --> 00:20:33,640
Is that true?

172
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:36,600
My father gives me complete freedom

173
00:20:36,680 --> 00:20:38,600
when it comes to my policies and ideas.

174
00:20:39,560 --> 00:20:42,760
I want everyone to trust
that I genuinely intend

175
00:20:42,840 --> 00:20:44,680
to improve lives in this community.

176
00:20:45,240 --> 00:20:48,880
I want everyone to live better
and have enough to support themselves.

177
00:20:48,960 --> 00:20:52,240
And I will make this Subdistrict Office
free of corruption.

178
00:20:52,800 --> 00:20:54,320
Vote number one.

179
00:20:54,400 --> 00:20:58,000
Congratulations to candidate number one.

180
00:20:58,960 --> 00:21:00,080
Thank you.

181
00:21:00,160 --> 00:21:02,600
Is Miss Chayanee,
Mr. Pichai's granddaughter,

182
00:21:02,680 --> 00:21:05,280
also one of your major supporters?

183
00:21:05,360 --> 00:21:06,960
-Chayanee--
-Yes.

184
00:21:09,560 --> 00:21:11,320
I'm Raiwin's girlfriend,

185
00:21:11,400 --> 00:21:13,680
and I'm ready to support him
in everything.

186
00:21:14,280 --> 00:21:17,800
The two of us will work hand in hand
to make this a better community.

187
00:21:17,880 --> 00:21:19,520
Please support us.

188
00:21:19,600 --> 00:21:21,400
Raiwin, number one.

189
00:21:21,480 --> 00:21:23,680
Please support us.

190
00:21:23,760 --> 00:21:25,680
Remember number one. He's my son.

191
00:21:25,760 --> 00:21:28,760
If there's ever anything
I can do for you, just let me know.

192
00:21:28,840 --> 00:21:32,160
Number one. Okay?

193
00:21:36,120 --> 00:21:37,840
I'm taking you for a luck ritual.

194
00:21:37,920 --> 00:21:41,680
I know a shrine that never fails.
Everyone who goes there succeeds.

195
00:21:43,360 --> 00:21:48,000
I think success is more about good
policies and getting out to meet people.

196
00:21:48,080 --> 00:21:50,440
We need to earn their trust.

197
00:21:50,520 --> 00:21:53,080
But spiritual rituals matter too.

198
00:21:53,160 --> 00:21:56,360
Don't disrespect what you don't
believe in. I already set your schedule.

199
00:21:56,440 --> 00:21:57,680
I got my candidate number.

200
00:21:57,760 --> 00:22:00,280
I need to meet voters.
I have no time for that.

201
00:22:00,360 --> 00:22:03,000
If you want to do the rituals,
you can do them for me.

202
00:22:03,880 --> 00:22:06,880
What is wrong with you?
You oppose everything I say.

203
00:22:07,600 --> 00:22:10,240
I'm not trying to oppose with you.
I just don't agree.

204
00:22:10,840 --> 00:22:14,320
And I also wasn't happy about you stealing
the spotlight during the interview.

205
00:22:16,960 --> 00:22:18,240
You're angry with me?

206
00:22:21,640 --> 00:22:25,360
I'm not angry.

207
00:22:26,080 --> 00:22:28,480
But I wasn't okay with it. Instead

208
00:22:28,560 --> 00:22:31,000
of giving me room to promote myself,

209
00:22:31,520 --> 00:22:34,760
you took over
and answered everything for me.

210
00:22:35,360 --> 00:22:38,120
Chayanee.

211
00:22:38,200 --> 00:22:41,800
You came all this way
to congratulate Raiwin.

212
00:22:41,880 --> 00:22:42,760
Why don't we all

213
00:22:42,840 --> 00:22:45,880
go get something good to eat?

214
00:22:45,960 --> 00:22:48,680
We can celebrate in advance.

215
00:22:48,760 --> 00:22:50,000
I'm not going.

216
00:22:51,520 --> 00:22:54,480
What happened?

217
00:22:54,560 --> 00:22:58,600
Ask your son. He says
I stole the spotlight from him

218
00:22:58,680 --> 00:23:01,040
when I was only trying
to help build his support base.

219
00:23:01,120 --> 00:23:03,520
People today need to work as a team.

220
00:23:05,680 --> 00:23:06,800
And don't forget.

221
00:23:07,320 --> 00:23:09,600
Every baht you're spending

222
00:23:09,680 --> 00:23:13,520
on registering and campaigning
is my money.

223
00:23:15,440 --> 00:23:19,280
If you think I'm embarrassing you,

224
00:23:19,360 --> 00:23:20,920
then maybe I won't get involved.

225
00:23:23,800 --> 00:23:27,320
Why don't we all calm down
and talk about this?

226
00:23:27,400 --> 00:23:29,120
And you too, Uncle.

227
00:23:29,840 --> 00:23:33,440
All the customers you sent us
last time couldn't get financing.

228
00:23:34,400 --> 00:23:37,680
Next time, please send
higher-class customers.

229
00:23:37,760 --> 00:23:39,320
I don't want low-end customers.

230
00:23:49,880 --> 00:23:51,200
She's so spoiled.

231
00:23:52,400 --> 00:23:53,400
Hey.

232
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:57,840
Raiwin, go after Chayanee
and apologize right now.

233
00:23:57,920 --> 00:23:59,240
Dad.

234
00:23:59,840 --> 00:24:02,720
She just insulted you. And you still
want me to go apologize to her?

235
00:24:02,800 --> 00:24:06,680
Every election costs money.

236
00:24:06,760 --> 00:24:09,080
It isn't won
with your ridiculous fantasy policies.

237
00:24:10,200 --> 00:24:12,520
I told you. I'm not selling fantasies.

238
00:24:12,600 --> 00:24:15,160
I'm offering ideas
for improving the community.

239
00:24:17,080 --> 00:24:20,760
I've been a politician my entire life.

240
00:24:20,840 --> 00:24:23,480
I know what voters like
and what they don't.

241
00:24:23,560 --> 00:24:26,280
They won't even read
those ridiculous policies of yours.

242
00:24:26,880 --> 00:24:28,520
They vote for the person with money.

243
00:24:28,600 --> 00:24:31,400
That's real life, son.

244
00:24:35,720 --> 00:24:38,400
If you don't have campaign money,

245
00:24:38,480 --> 00:24:39,880
you've already lost.

246
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:42,200
Go on.

247
00:24:42,280 --> 00:24:45,400
Go apologize to Chayanee right now. Go.

248
00:24:45,480 --> 00:24:48,880
I said go. Now.

249
00:24:58,240 --> 00:24:59,200
I'm sorry.

250
00:25:00,160 --> 00:25:03,680
Nothing I do is ever good enough.
Don't waste your time on me.

251
00:25:04,680 --> 00:25:05,800
Chayanee.

252
00:25:10,080 --> 00:25:12,920
I'm sorry. I love you.

253
00:25:14,760 --> 00:25:16,760
I love you too.

254
00:25:21,040 --> 00:25:23,720
Everything I do is for you.

255
00:25:25,080 --> 00:25:27,880
Promise me you won't hurt me again.

256
00:25:31,200 --> 00:25:35,000
Say it. Promise me
you won't go against me again.

257
00:25:39,440 --> 00:25:40,360
I promise.

258
00:25:43,440 --> 00:25:45,640
I love my future Chief more than anything.

259
00:25:48,400 --> 00:25:49,480
Let's go.

260
00:26:13,440 --> 00:26:16,360
Madam, are you really going to let Hathai

261
00:26:16,440 --> 00:26:18,440
stay here and walk all over you?

262
00:26:18,520 --> 00:26:21,800
Just think about it.
Mr. Pichai already trusts Hathaya,

263
00:26:21,880 --> 00:26:25,320
and now her mother has moved in too.
They'll be twice as manipulative.

264
00:26:25,400 --> 00:26:28,080
What if Mr. Pichai leaves
his inheritance to them?

265
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:33,520
Shut up. I've already
been thinking about it so much

266
00:26:33,600 --> 00:26:35,800
I'm getting a migraine.

267
00:26:35,880 --> 00:26:37,440
Madam.

268
00:26:37,520 --> 00:26:39,640
I'm only worried about you.

269
00:26:39,720 --> 00:26:43,520
I'm getting a migraine too.
My head is throbbing.

270
00:26:43,600 --> 00:26:47,120
At least Father still
hasn't forgiven Hathai.

271
00:26:47,200 --> 00:26:48,760
But we can't let our guard down.

272
00:26:48,840 --> 00:26:52,400
Those people are like
venomous snakes waiting to strike.

273
00:26:53,520 --> 00:26:57,360
Then we have to get rid of them
and send them far away.

274
00:26:57,440 --> 00:26:59,360
You think they're bags of garbage

275
00:26:59,440 --> 00:27:01,960
we can just throw out?

276
00:27:02,960 --> 00:27:05,560
Then we have to pressure them.

277
00:27:05,640 --> 00:27:07,960
Make things unbearable for them.

278
00:27:09,360 --> 00:27:12,280
Then we make

279
00:27:12,360 --> 00:27:14,240
Father think they're bad people.

280
00:27:16,200 --> 00:27:17,640
How are you going to do that?

281
00:27:30,840 --> 00:27:33,720
Brilliant. Absolutely brilliant.

282
00:27:33,800 --> 00:27:35,600
That idea is downright evil.

283
00:27:38,280 --> 00:27:40,200
-That was a compliment, right?
-Absolutely.

284
00:27:47,880 --> 00:27:48,920
What are you making?

285
00:27:50,080 --> 00:27:51,800
Rice porridge for Grandpa.

286
00:27:52,440 --> 00:27:53,520
Want me to help?

287
00:27:57,240 --> 00:28:00,400
Actually, maybe I shouldn't.

288
00:28:00,480 --> 00:28:02,640
If Grandpa finds out,
he might get angry again.

289
00:28:05,840 --> 00:28:07,000
Come on, Mom.

290
00:28:07,880 --> 00:28:11,520
Help me. Your cooking is better than mine.

291
00:28:11,600 --> 00:28:12,920
Then let's do it.

292
00:28:13,600 --> 00:28:15,040
Ms. Hathai

293
00:28:15,600 --> 00:28:19,560
used to cook almost every meal herself.

294
00:28:19,640 --> 00:28:23,200
I still miss your cooking.

295
00:28:23,960 --> 00:28:27,240
Thanks, Ann. You're always encouraging me.

296
00:28:30,400 --> 00:28:31,920
Let's do it together, Mom.

297
00:28:32,000 --> 00:28:34,400
You make the porridge,
and I'll prepare the seasonings.

298
00:28:38,280 --> 00:28:39,560
You're sure to make it delicious.

299
00:28:45,040 --> 00:28:48,560
Madam. I got it.

300
00:28:48,640 --> 00:28:49,640
The good stuff.

301
00:28:54,360 --> 00:28:56,440
You're a genius, madam.

302
00:28:56,520 --> 00:29:00,000
If we put this in Hathaya
and her mother's food every day,

303
00:29:00,080 --> 00:29:02,280
they'll run out of this house before long.

304
00:29:03,320 --> 00:29:05,000
Think, Chamoi.

305
00:29:05,840 --> 00:29:08,120
How many days would we
have to keep giving it to them

306
00:29:08,200 --> 00:29:09,280
before they finally gave up?

307
00:29:11,400 --> 00:29:13,840
Well, probably a while.

308
00:29:13,920 --> 00:29:16,040
But I only need to use it once

309
00:29:16,760 --> 00:29:19,920
to get them thrown out of this house.

310
00:29:20,520 --> 00:29:21,480
How?

311
00:29:21,560 --> 00:29:25,160
We put it in the food
they made for Father.

312
00:29:26,560 --> 00:29:29,080
Madam. Then Mr. Pichai will--

313
00:29:30,200 --> 00:29:33,120
He'll just have to use the bathroom
a few times. It won't kill him.

314
00:29:33,760 --> 00:29:36,600
I already prepared
an electrolyte solution for him.

315
00:29:37,240 --> 00:29:38,640
Here. Take care of it.

316
00:29:38,720 --> 00:29:40,200
Yes, madam.

317
00:29:40,280 --> 00:29:42,080
Go.

318
00:29:47,600 --> 00:29:48,720
Aunt Liu, is something wrong?

319
00:29:48,800 --> 00:29:50,560
If you came for the food,

320
00:29:50,640 --> 00:29:53,160
Mom and I just finished.
We were about to take it to Grandpa.

321
00:29:54,320 --> 00:29:55,520
I know

322
00:29:55,600 --> 00:29:58,520
you two cook so well

323
00:29:59,320 --> 00:30:02,840
that Father loves everything you make.
Everything you do pleases him.

324
00:30:03,440 --> 00:30:06,000
What do you want? Just say it.

325
00:30:11,280 --> 00:30:14,720
Father barely speaks to me anymore.

326
00:30:16,080 --> 00:30:18,000
I just want to help with something.

327
00:30:18,760 --> 00:30:21,240
Here. Give it to me.
I'll help carry it to Father.

328
00:30:21,320 --> 00:30:23,720
Don't. They can't be trusted.

329
00:30:23,800 --> 00:30:24,800
What's that?

330
00:30:24,880 --> 00:30:27,280
She said you two look suspicious.

331
00:30:29,680 --> 00:30:31,280
But I don't think so.

332
00:30:32,120 --> 00:30:36,000
I know you love and care
about Father just as much as we do.

333
00:30:42,680 --> 00:30:44,080
Let's take it to Grandpa.

334
00:30:57,680 --> 00:30:58,960
Hurry.

335
00:30:59,040 --> 00:31:01,200
-It'll give him the runs.
-Quickly.

336
00:31:02,000 --> 00:31:02,960
More.

337
00:31:03,040 --> 00:31:05,760
This is already enough
to send someone running to the bathroom.

338
00:31:06,360 --> 00:31:09,880
Make sure it works. I want Father
to be furious with them.

339
00:31:09,960 --> 00:31:12,520
-Pour in more.
-The whole bottle?

340
00:31:17,600 --> 00:31:19,280
Is something wrong?

341
00:31:19,360 --> 00:31:20,520
Why aren't you coming?

342
00:31:21,240 --> 00:31:22,720
You're so slow.

343
00:31:22,800 --> 00:31:24,320
Hurry up. Father must be hungry.

344
00:31:24,400 --> 00:31:26,200
Yes.

345
00:31:32,080 --> 00:31:33,320
Oh!

346
00:31:35,840 --> 00:31:37,160
What is it?

347
00:31:37,920 --> 00:31:39,680
Aunt Liu, come sit and eat with us.

348
00:31:41,320 --> 00:31:42,480
Father.

349
00:31:42,560 --> 00:31:44,600
Why don't you eat this bowl instead?

350
00:31:44,680 --> 00:31:46,640
Hathai and Hathaya

351
00:31:46,720 --> 00:31:49,120
made it especially for you.

352
00:31:50,000 --> 00:31:53,280
But that bowl

353
00:31:53,360 --> 00:31:55,120
came from the same pot Mom and I made.

354
00:31:55,200 --> 00:31:59,040
I brought Grandpa his bowl first
so he could take his medicine on time.

355
00:31:59,120 --> 00:32:00,200
Oh.

356
00:32:00,720 --> 00:32:03,080
Father probably isn't full yet.

357
00:32:03,160 --> 00:32:06,520
Have another bowl.
Then you can take your medicine.

358
00:32:06,600 --> 00:32:08,920
I'm full. I'm taking my medicine now.

359
00:32:12,000 --> 00:32:14,440
What a shame.
There's still another bowl left.

360
00:32:16,760 --> 00:32:17,880
Then eat it yourself.

361
00:32:25,320 --> 00:32:26,200
What?

362
00:32:28,160 --> 00:32:33,040
It's okay, Father. I'm already full.

363
00:32:33,120 --> 00:32:36,400
I'll give this bowl to Chamoi.

364
00:32:36,480 --> 00:32:38,080
Eat it.

365
00:32:38,160 --> 00:32:40,360
I'm full too, sir.

366
00:32:40,440 --> 00:32:43,480
I was tasting the food while we made it.
I'm completely stuffed.

367
00:32:44,080 --> 00:32:46,920
Why make such a big deal
about eating together?

368
00:32:47,000 --> 00:32:48,600
Just take it away.

369
00:32:48,680 --> 00:32:50,880
Aunt Liu.

370
00:32:51,760 --> 00:32:53,120
Are you still angry with Mom?

371
00:32:55,120 --> 00:32:58,520
Mom put a lot of effort
into making this porridge.

372
00:32:58,600 --> 00:33:00,040
Come eat with us.

373
00:33:02,760 --> 00:33:04,520
I'm really not hungry.

374
00:33:05,120 --> 00:33:07,680
Stop standing over everyone.
Sit down and eat.

375
00:33:09,600 --> 00:33:12,440
Are you going to refuse Grandpa?

376
00:33:16,520 --> 00:33:18,920
Please sit.

377
00:33:42,560 --> 00:33:45,200
Such a tiny bite.

378
00:33:45,280 --> 00:33:47,760
That's not very respectful, Liu.

379
00:33:54,040 --> 00:33:55,480
Yes.

380
00:33:58,560 --> 00:34:01,640
Madam, take a big bite.

381
00:34:01,720 --> 00:34:03,400
Show some spirit.

382
00:34:20,239 --> 00:34:22,000
Delicious.

383
00:34:23,199 --> 00:34:25,280
If it's delicious, finish the whole bowl.

384
00:34:27,800 --> 00:34:29,719
Have plenty.

385
00:34:38,440 --> 00:34:39,920
Delicious.

386
00:34:41,560 --> 00:34:46,040
Aunt Liu, why do you look so nauseated?

387
00:34:46,120 --> 00:34:49,239
You're acting like there's poison
in that porridge.

388
00:34:49,320 --> 00:34:52,320
What poison? There's nothing in it.

389
00:34:52,400 --> 00:34:55,560
It's just rice porridge. Delicious.

390
00:34:57,480 --> 00:34:59,640
Then eat plenty.

391
00:34:59,720 --> 00:35:01,120
Finish the bowl.

392
00:35:17,080 --> 00:35:18,040
What's wrong?

393
00:35:18,640 --> 00:35:20,160
Nothing.

394
00:35:31,800 --> 00:35:32,920
Actually, something's wrong.

395
00:35:34,280 --> 00:35:35,400
Excuse me.

396
00:35:41,520 --> 00:35:45,360
Sir, may I go check on Madam?

397
00:35:46,880 --> 00:35:48,760
What is wrong with Liu today?

398
00:35:49,400 --> 00:35:51,640
Getting up and leaving like that. So rude.

399
00:35:51,720 --> 00:35:54,080
She may not be feeling well, Grandpa.

400
00:35:54,160 --> 00:35:57,880
If you're finished eating, you should
rest. I'll take care of everything here.

401
00:36:16,120 --> 00:36:17,520
Come on, sweetheart. Keep eating.

402
00:36:21,080 --> 00:36:22,560
Madam.

403
00:36:25,040 --> 00:36:28,480
Are you okay?

404
00:36:30,160 --> 00:36:32,720
I only ate a few bites.

405
00:36:32,800 --> 00:36:34,160
How could it be this bad?

406
00:36:35,360 --> 00:36:39,040
That means the medicine really works.

407
00:36:39,120 --> 00:36:41,640
What a great product.
I should go leave them a review.

408
00:36:41,720 --> 00:36:42,920
You idiot.

409
00:36:44,520 --> 00:36:47,880
Madam? Are you okay?

410
00:36:48,480 --> 00:36:49,600
I don't…

411
00:36:51,160 --> 00:36:52,400
think I…

412
00:37:01,640 --> 00:37:03,920
I can't breathe, madam.

413
00:37:04,560 --> 00:37:05,760
I… can't--

414
00:37:12,960 --> 00:37:15,000
Sit down, madam.

415
00:37:16,720 --> 00:37:20,480
-Are you okay?
-There's nothing left inside me.

416
00:37:20,560 --> 00:37:22,200
I don't even have the strength

417
00:37:22,280 --> 00:37:24,160
to breathe.

418
00:37:24,240 --> 00:37:26,160
Madam.

419
00:37:26,240 --> 00:37:28,160
You have to breathe.

420
00:37:28,240 --> 00:37:30,480
If you stop breathing, you'll die.

421
00:37:31,880 --> 00:37:34,880
Help me. I have no strength left.

422
00:37:34,960 --> 00:37:37,480
Come on.

423
00:37:37,560 --> 00:37:38,800
-I can't--
-Aunt Liu,

424
00:37:39,360 --> 00:37:40,800
here's some electrolyte solution

425
00:37:42,240 --> 00:37:44,400
for the diarrhea. Sip it slowly.

426
00:37:44,480 --> 00:37:45,880
It helps replace lost fluids.

427
00:37:46,760 --> 00:37:49,880
You knew?

428
00:37:51,320 --> 00:37:54,160
Yes. I knew what you were planning.

429
00:37:54,720 --> 00:37:58,120
We put this medicine into the food
they made for Father.

430
00:37:58,200 --> 00:37:59,240
Yes.

431
00:37:59,760 --> 00:38:01,840
Go.

432
00:38:08,600 --> 00:38:10,400
You knew what I was doing?

433
00:38:10,480 --> 00:38:11,720
Then why didn't you stop me?

434
00:38:12,720 --> 00:38:16,600
If we had stopped you, you wouldn't
have learned your lesson.

435
00:38:17,200 --> 00:38:19,320
The moral of this story is simple.

436
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:21,640
The suffering you cause others

437
00:38:21,720 --> 00:38:23,760
comes back to you.

438
00:38:26,840 --> 00:38:30,040
You two are evil.
Both mother and daughter.

439
00:38:30,120 --> 00:38:33,200
If we're evil, then what
do you call what you did?

440
00:38:35,040 --> 00:38:37,320
You wanted revenge on us,

441
00:38:37,400 --> 00:38:38,920
but you used Father as your weapon.

442
00:38:41,440 --> 00:38:43,480
Think about

443
00:38:43,560 --> 00:38:46,800
what would happen if he found out.

444
00:38:48,880 --> 00:38:51,000
Don't. Please.

445
00:38:53,240 --> 00:38:55,880
I don't want Father
getting any more stressed.

446
00:38:56,920 --> 00:38:58,600
So stop this.

447
00:38:59,400 --> 00:39:00,760
Because if you don't,

448
00:39:01,680 --> 00:39:03,960
the people leaving this house

449
00:39:04,600 --> 00:39:06,000
won't be us.

450
00:39:06,840 --> 00:39:08,200
It'll be you.

451
00:39:10,760 --> 00:39:12,000
Let's go.

452
00:39:12,080 --> 00:39:13,280
Do you understand?

453
00:39:14,800 --> 00:39:15,960
Yes.

454
00:39:16,040 --> 00:39:18,240
I understood you from the first sentence.

455
00:39:19,560 --> 00:39:21,200
Let's go, madam.

456
00:39:25,880 --> 00:39:28,360
Madam, please sit.

457
00:39:28,440 --> 00:39:29,520
Too late.

458
00:39:31,120 --> 00:39:34,760
Madam, I can taste that smell.

459
00:39:42,480 --> 00:39:44,920
Thank you, Mom, for protecting me.

460
00:39:46,080 --> 00:39:47,960
You don't have to thank me.

461
00:39:48,040 --> 00:39:51,560
That's a mother's job.
I should've done this long ago.

462
00:39:52,080 --> 00:39:54,880
I'm the one who should apologize to you

463
00:39:54,960 --> 00:39:56,960
for never being a good mother.

464
00:39:57,560 --> 00:40:00,960
Forget about the past, Mom.
It's not too late to start over.

465
00:40:04,480 --> 00:40:08,200
I wonder when Grandpa will finally

466
00:40:08,280 --> 00:40:11,480
forgive me and soften toward me.

467
00:40:12,360 --> 00:40:15,320
There's only one way to win Grandpa over.

468
00:40:15,400 --> 00:40:19,000
Be sincere. You have to be patient.

469
00:40:20,560 --> 00:40:21,560
I will.

470
00:40:26,520 --> 00:40:27,800
Those roses are beautiful.

471
00:40:30,240 --> 00:40:33,440
Grandma Duangjai planted them herself.

472
00:40:39,040 --> 00:40:42,280
Grandma wanted to grow roses
to brighten Grandpa's day.

473
00:40:42,360 --> 00:40:44,640
That way there would
always be fragrant roses

474
00:40:45,280 --> 00:40:47,000
for his vase.

475
00:41:03,840 --> 00:41:05,040
Mom.

476
00:41:07,520 --> 00:41:09,040
From now on,

477
00:41:09,760 --> 00:41:12,400
I'll take care of this
rose garden for you.

478
00:41:18,000 --> 00:41:19,640
And I'll take the best

479
00:41:20,480 --> 00:41:22,160
possible care of my daughter too.

480
00:41:26,880 --> 00:41:28,880
You don't have to worry
about either of us.

481
00:41:47,120 --> 00:41:50,000
Now that Grandpa put you in charge
of all construction sections,

482
00:41:50,080 --> 00:41:51,320
are you exhausted?

483
00:41:52,880 --> 00:41:56,280
I'll admit I'm tired,
but I have more peace of mind.

484
00:41:57,600 --> 00:41:58,920
How so?

485
00:41:59,000 --> 00:42:00,720
Lots of work in the areas Pong supervised

486
00:42:00,800 --> 00:42:04,240
must be torn out and redone.
But don't worry.

487
00:42:04,320 --> 00:42:05,480
We'll still finish on time.

488
00:42:06,080 --> 00:42:07,600
Thank you for helping.

489
00:42:15,000 --> 00:42:16,920
I brought lunch for everyone.

490
00:42:17,000 --> 00:42:19,520
Mom makes amazing
rice noodles with spicy curry.

491
00:42:19,600 --> 00:42:21,280
I thought everyone might like it.

492
00:42:23,480 --> 00:42:25,880
Just smelling it is making me hungry.

493
00:42:29,040 --> 00:42:31,680
Everyone. Miss Hathaya

494
00:42:31,760 --> 00:42:34,400
is treating us to rice noodles
for lunch today.

495
00:42:34,480 --> 00:42:37,280
Eat up, and then make sure
we finish the work on schedule.

496
00:42:37,360 --> 00:42:40,320
-Yes, boss. Thank you.
-Thank you.

497
00:42:43,480 --> 00:42:45,160
-You want some?
-Yes.

498
00:42:46,200 --> 00:42:47,080
NUMBER 1
RAIWIN TRAIPONGRATCHATA

499
00:42:47,160 --> 00:42:49,240
You all live around here.

500
00:42:49,320 --> 00:42:50,960
Please support Raiwin.

501
00:42:51,560 --> 00:42:52,960
And

502
00:42:54,240 --> 00:42:57,640
-hand these out to customers.
-Of course, Miss Chayanee.

503
00:42:57,720 --> 00:42:58,640
Let's go.

504
00:43:06,600 --> 00:43:07,640
Where did Raiwin go?

505
00:43:14,360 --> 00:43:15,800
Hello, beautiful vendor.

506
00:43:16,440 --> 00:43:19,160
I haven't eaten anything yet.
Can I have some too?

507
00:43:20,680 --> 00:43:24,120
Let me get some curry for you.

508
00:43:39,920 --> 00:43:41,400
That looks delicious.

509
00:43:44,200 --> 00:43:45,400
Hathaya.

510
00:43:47,080 --> 00:43:49,160
Would you be one
of my campaign canvassers?

511
00:43:51,280 --> 00:43:54,400
I'd rather not.
Politics really isn't my thing.

512
00:43:55,160 --> 00:43:57,000
You're the perfect person for it.

513
00:43:57,520 --> 00:43:58,920
You're capable.

514
00:43:59,000 --> 00:44:01,360
Both the workers and people
around here really like you.

515
00:44:02,400 --> 00:44:04,080
If you help campaign for me,

516
00:44:04,160 --> 00:44:07,520
I'm sure I'll win.

517
00:44:10,680 --> 00:44:13,640
Please. I'm asking you, Hathaya.

518
00:44:15,200 --> 00:44:16,320
What are you doing?

519
00:44:20,520 --> 00:44:23,160
I came to campaign among the workers.

520
00:44:23,760 --> 00:44:25,640
I was asking Hathaya
to help canvass for me.

521
00:44:25,720 --> 00:44:28,040
You don't need Hathaya.

522
00:44:28,120 --> 00:44:29,520
She's an outsider.

523
00:44:31,560 --> 00:44:34,760
I was born here. I'm from here.

524
00:44:35,560 --> 00:44:37,000
My reputation is more than enough

525
00:44:37,080 --> 00:44:39,480
to get everyone to vote for you.

526
00:44:39,560 --> 00:44:42,200
You don't need to rely on anyone else.

527
00:44:42,720 --> 00:44:45,960
Besides, Hathaya comes from
the lower class.

528
00:44:46,520 --> 00:44:48,000
You can't rely on people like that.

529
00:44:51,080 --> 00:44:52,680
Then why don't you

530
00:44:52,760 --> 00:44:54,880
help me campaign around here?

531
00:44:54,960 --> 00:44:57,680
You said you came to campaign
among the workers, didn't you?

532
00:44:57,760 --> 00:45:00,080
Then go. Hand out your flyers.

533
00:45:01,920 --> 00:45:03,880
All right. Come with me.

534
00:45:07,000 --> 00:45:10,880
That curry looks good.
I'm going to have some first.

535
00:45:10,960 --> 00:45:12,520
You go ahead.

536
00:45:14,760 --> 00:45:16,160
Go.

537
00:45:26,080 --> 00:45:27,080
Ramil.

538
00:45:28,880 --> 00:45:31,320
-Do me a favor.
-What?

539
00:45:32,800 --> 00:45:35,760
Ask Hathaya to help campaign for me.

540
00:45:37,200 --> 00:45:39,560
I think you should ask Hathaya yourself.

541
00:45:40,440 --> 00:45:42,440
But she listens to you.

542
00:45:43,120 --> 00:45:44,640
Help me this once.

543
00:45:44,720 --> 00:45:46,920
Consider it repayment
for the favor I did for you.

544
00:45:48,080 --> 00:45:50,200
I think

545
00:45:50,280 --> 00:45:53,640
Chayanee might have a problem
with Hathaya helping you.

546
00:45:54,760 --> 00:45:56,720
Then don't let Chayanee know.

547
00:45:58,080 --> 00:46:00,440
I don't like her interfering
in my business.

548
00:46:00,520 --> 00:46:02,960
Just talk to Hathaya for me.

549
00:46:09,120 --> 00:46:10,760
This curry is spicy,

550
00:46:10,840 --> 00:46:13,160
but apparently not spicy enough for you.

551
00:46:13,240 --> 00:46:15,000
So you're trying to get a taste of my man?

552
00:46:15,880 --> 00:46:18,080
Chaya, what are you talking about?

553
00:46:18,160 --> 00:46:20,120
If I'd arrived a little later,

554
00:46:20,200 --> 00:46:22,240
you two would've snuck off somewhere here.

555
00:46:22,320 --> 00:46:25,040
Chayanee. I've never thought
about him that way.

556
00:46:25,120 --> 00:46:26,440
Never thought about it?

557
00:46:26,520 --> 00:46:28,360
Or you just never had the chance?

558
00:46:29,240 --> 00:46:30,960
You used to like Raiwin.

559
00:46:31,960 --> 00:46:33,560
Then you ended up with Ramil instead.

560
00:46:34,240 --> 00:46:36,960
What? That rough man

561
00:46:37,040 --> 00:46:40,160
doesn't satisfy you, so now you
want another taste of my Raiwin?

562
00:46:42,360 --> 00:46:43,800
Hathaya,

563
00:46:45,000 --> 00:46:46,360
if you like things spicy,

564
00:46:46,440 --> 00:46:49,040
then I'll pour some curry on you
to make it really burn.

565
00:46:51,760 --> 00:46:53,480
Stop thinking such disgusting things.

566
00:46:55,760 --> 00:46:57,560
I have never wanted another woman's man.

567
00:46:59,480 --> 00:47:01,800
Rather than wasting time being jealous,

568
00:47:01,880 --> 00:47:03,800
go take care of your own man.

569
00:47:05,760 --> 00:47:07,600
I spoke to Raiwin

570
00:47:07,680 --> 00:47:11,040
because I respect him
as Ramil's older brother.

571
00:47:11,600 --> 00:47:12,640
And

572
00:47:13,160 --> 00:47:15,040
don't worry about me trying to steal him.

573
00:47:15,640 --> 00:47:18,000
I don't take another woman's man.

574
00:47:18,080 --> 00:47:19,280
I'm not like you.

575
00:47:19,360 --> 00:47:20,200
Hathaya.

576
00:47:20,280 --> 00:47:22,560
If you want to help Raiwin campaign,

577
00:47:22,640 --> 00:47:25,560
then behave properly. Act like
the wealthy heiress you claim to be.

578
00:47:27,160 --> 00:47:30,240
Throwing tantrums and screaming
in public isn't a good look.

579
00:47:33,080 --> 00:47:34,320
Raiwin.

580
00:47:37,640 --> 00:47:39,880
I called you. Didn't you hear me?

581
00:47:41,680 --> 00:47:42,520
Go.

582
00:47:51,760 --> 00:47:53,040
What is it?

583
00:48:13,840 --> 00:48:15,000
What was that?

584
00:48:16,000 --> 00:48:18,480
Did Chayanee say something that upset you?

585
00:48:19,520 --> 00:48:21,040
She's jealous of me.

586
00:48:22,200 --> 00:48:23,880
She thinks I'm stealing Raiwin.

587
00:48:31,960 --> 00:48:33,160
Why did you call me?

588
00:48:37,360 --> 00:48:38,720
What was that for?

589
00:48:41,240 --> 00:48:43,520
-Chayanee.
-Don't raise your voice at me.

590
00:48:44,760 --> 00:48:46,320
I'm knocking some sense into you.

591
00:48:47,040 --> 00:48:48,800
If I call for you,

592
00:48:48,880 --> 00:48:50,520
you come to me immediately.

593
00:48:50,600 --> 00:48:52,920
Don't make me call you twice.
You're embarrassing me.

594
00:48:53,000 --> 00:48:55,040
And you think I'm not embarrassed?

595
00:48:55,120 --> 00:48:57,800
You shouted my name
like I was your servant.

596
00:48:57,880 --> 00:48:59,760
You're not my servant.

597
00:49:00,320 --> 00:49:03,320
But you belong to me. Not Hathaya.

598
00:49:09,760 --> 00:49:13,080
Chayanee is jealous of me.
She thinks I'm stealing Raiwin.

599
00:49:13,160 --> 00:49:14,640
If I'd arrived a little later,

600
00:49:14,720 --> 00:49:16,280
you two would've snuck off somewhere.

601
00:49:16,360 --> 00:49:18,160
Ramil, you don't deserve this.

602
00:49:18,760 --> 00:49:20,800
I want you to get close to Hathai

603
00:49:20,880 --> 00:49:23,160
and lure her into your trap.

604
00:49:23,240 --> 00:49:24,160
NEXT EPISODE

605
00:49:24,240 --> 00:49:25,160
You know

606
00:49:25,240 --> 00:49:28,000
I'm good at getting close to women.

607
00:49:28,080 --> 00:49:30,480
Raiwin asked me to talk to you.

608
00:49:30,560 --> 00:49:32,120
He wants you to help campaign for him.

609
00:49:32,200 --> 00:49:33,080
Mr. Saksit,

610
00:49:33,160 --> 00:49:34,920
do you even realize what you're doing?

611
00:49:35,520 --> 00:49:37,400
You're hurting your own son.

612
00:51:29,520 --> 00:51:33,680
Subtitle translation by: Thanit Puncharoen
